cpr-plugin-bps implements BPS natively in Rust. No Go executable or HTTP
bridge is included or required at runtime.

The BPS protocol implementation is adapted from:
https://github.com/sunboyzoey/bps-local-public
commit 7134964fe0ce72b6b44b000cc97d86ea1e7b80e5

Sources used: internal/basispoints/{request,content,catalog,tools,envelope,
plan,stream,structured_output,configuration_history,images,custom_transport}.go and
internal/{auth/{auth,device},proxy/websocket}.go

Original Basispoints changes: hloolx
Upstream baseline: Unlicense; upstream describes protocol changes as MIT,
but notes that complete original/intermediate notices have not been verified.
The upstream license collection is preserved in licenses/bps-local.txt;
no claim of independent license verification is made.

This port changes implementation language, integrates the public CPR SDK,
uses host-managed network and private state, strengthens replay isolation,
and replaces the standalone HTTP server with native upstream-adapter events.
It does not include the upstream Go dependency implementations. Their texts
remain in the preserved license collection as part of the upstream notice.

gateway-plugin-sdk is consumed from codex-proxy-rs under Apache-2.0.
The management page consumes @codex-proxy/ui v0.8.0 under Apache-2.0.
Its license is preserved in licenses/codex-proxy-ui.txt; its source was not modified.
This plugin is unofficial and is not affiliated with OpenAI or Codex Proxy RS.
